          "content": {
            "content_type": "text",
            "parts": [
              "Yes—the results justify a **methods paper**, although they do not establish a new general theta-positivity range or resolve RH. I consolidated them into a checked, 24-page draft.\n\nThe main results are:\n\n- **Exact Green identities** retaining every boundary contribution, with a complete determinant-error calculation.\n- **Three certified finite bounds:** \\(Q_{3,1}>7\\times10^{-23}\\), \\(Q_{3,4}>10^{-74}\\), and \\(Q_{4,1}>3\\times10^{-31}\\).\n- **Precise limitations of earlier references:** fixed-pole references eventually vanish in specified dimensions; the Gaussian reference cannot support fixed uniform relative slack.\n- **A growth-matched pair reference**, together with algebraic controls showing that an \\(O(q^{-2})\\) coefficient error can coexist with a negative diagonal determinant. These are not theta counterexamples.\n\nSol’s completed assessment accepted all twelve latest obligations within scope, without mathematical correction. That return is incorporated; the review remains internal LLM assessment.\n\n:codex-file-citation{path=\"/Users/ebbaker/Documents/shifted-zeta-positivity/output/pdf/radial-green-determinants/radial_green_determinants.pdf\" purpose=\"output\"}\n\nThe [editable manuscript](/Users/ebbaker/Documents/shifted-zeta-positivity/papers/investigations-5/07_positive_theta_primitives/01_jensen/01_mellin_curvature/10_radial_green_determinants/manuscript/radial_green_determinants.tex), research synthesis, progress register and milestone history are saved. Final chat capture is queued.\n\n**Next: [E] RGD-E04 r8 — Sol**, reviewing the assembled manuscript before further research. The [continuation and model-change guide](/Users/ebbaker/Documents/shifted-zeta-positivity/papers/investigations-5/07_positive_theta_primitives/01_jensen/01_mellin_curvature/10_radial_green_determinants/research-progress/handoffs/RGD_E04_R8_MANUSCRIPT_ASSESSMENT_AND_MODEL_CONTINUATION_20261104.md) contains the bounded review instructions."
